This game, despite being a slenderman clone, had some potential, but the execution kills it.
Pros:
The hat ghost was a good idea, it was more funny than scary for me;
The atmosphere was decent;
The gameplay is fun enough, almost 100% equal to the Slenderman game.
Cons:
Terrible map/level design: the player ends up getting lost in the maze of halls after about 1 minute of walking around;
2001 graphics: it's impossible for anything to be scary when the textures look like they were drawn in MSPaint;
The sounds and "scare" elements are cheap and cliché;
Confusing: there are no clues about where you should go or what should you do, besides wandering in search of notebook pages;
The Hatman is not a good enemy: you can always outrun him by far, so you only lose when you enter a room and then he's suddenly by the door, blocking your path.
Overall: 3/10

